  /* Preserve original semantics exactly.
     Key property: For each (i,j), updates C[k][j] for k<i create loop-carried
     dependences across i, so parallelizing i or j would race/alter results.
     We therefore keep i sequential and exploit safe parallelism over j
     with per-column privatization of C[*][j].

     Approach:
     - For each column j, compute the full sequential i=0..M-1 evolution of that column.
     - Use a thread-local buffer colC[0..M-1] initialized from C[:,j].
     - Perform all updates into colC, then write back to C[:,j].
     This is race-free and preserves the per-column order of updates. */

  const int Mloc = _PB_M;
  const int Nloc = _PB_N;

